  "reason": "Evidence: config_005 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, weighted) is the best result at 0.5318 acc, outperforming RNA-only (0.4849) and image-only (0.2266), confirming that the image modality adds complementary value when fused with pca_n2000. However, the fusion method (weighted) has not been compared against an alternative. Question: config_040 is identical to config_005 except fusion is changed from weighted to concat, providing a clean single-variable A/B test of the fusion strategy. Why this is the best next experiment: understanding whether concat or weighted fusion is superior is a foundational design decision that will inform all subsequent multimodal experiments (multiprofile, different encoders, aggregation). A single-variable comparison isolates the fusion effect without confounding from profile setting, encoder choice, or aggregation changes, making the result maximally interpretable under a limited budget."
